short_trace:
\[
\operatorname{proj}_{\begin{pmatrix}5\\2\end{pmatrix}} \begin{pmatrix}x\\y\end{pmatrix}
= \frac{5x+2y}{29} \begin{pmatrix}5\\2\end{pmatrix}
\]
Let this equal \(\begin{pmatrix}-\frac{5}{2}\\-1\end{pmatrix}\), so
\[
\frac{5x+2y}{29} \begin{pmatrix}5\\2\end{pmatrix}
= \begin{pmatrix}-\frac{5}{2}\\-1\end{pmatrix}
\]
If \(\frac{5x+2y}{29} = k\), then
\[
5k = -\frac{5}{2} \Rightarrow k = -\frac{1}{2}
\]
Thus
\[
k = \frac{5x+2y}{29} = -\frac{1}{2} \Rightarrow 5x+2y = -\frac{29}{2}
\]
Solving for \(y\):
\[
5x+2y = -\frac{29}{2} \Rightarrow y = -\frac{5}{2}x - \frac{29}{4}
\]

Final answer: y = -\frac{5}{2} x - \frac{29}{4}

